  "title": "Native contradictions are parity contradictions",
  "subject": "Where hardness lives in networks of three-place knots: native sharing, hubs and memory",
  "conclusion": "In an unsatisfiable hub-free network of three-place knots, every knot whose removal keeps the network connected allows exactly half of its edge states, so every native contradiction is a set of parity systems joined by forced values, and native networks of every law are decided in polynomial time. Native contradictions are hard for resolution exactly when the law has a parity knot, while hubs carry NP-hardness.",
